WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:06:16.293 --> 00:06:17.544
Yeah, I...


00:06:17.627 --> 00:06:20.338
I can ask my mom when
she gets back on Thursday.


00:06:20.422 --> 00:06:23.091
I wouldn't ask my dad,
'cause he'll just say "no"


00:06:23.174 --> 00:06:25.886
and give some stupid
arbitrary reason why.


00:06:28.597 --> 00:06:29.723
You're sure it's okay, though?


00:06:29.806 --> 00:06:31.016
Yeah, of course.


00:06:31.725 --> 00:06:34.060
What are you gonna do tonight, though?


00:07:09.638 --> 00:07:11.348
Sarah?


00:09:10.258 --> 00:09:12.510
Fuck yourselves!


00:09:12.594 --> 00:09:17.140
Freak. Such a weirdo.


00:09:26.566 --> 00:09:27.942
Hey.


00:09:28.026 --> 00:09:30.236
- Hey.
- You okay?


00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:33.406
I'm gonna grab a coffee.
You want anything?


00:09:33.490 --> 00:09:35.158
Yeah, I'll have another.


00:11:01.286 --> 00:11:03.997
Sarah? Come on in.


00:11:08.459 --> 00:11:10.962
Have you ever had any
difficulty getting to sleep


00:11:11.045 --> 00:11:13.840
or staying asleep?


00:11:13.923 --> 00:11:17.343
Uh, lately. Yes.


00:11:17.427 --> 00:11:19.846
Okay.


00:11:19.929 --> 00:11:21.306
Do you drink coffee, tea,


00:11:21.389 --> 00:11:23.015
or any other caffeinated beverages?


00:11:23.099 --> 00:11:25.101
And if so, how many per day?


00:11:25.185 --> 00:11:27.103
Coffee.


00:11:27.187 --> 00:11:31.357
Usually I'll have about
three to six cups a day.


00:11:31.482 --> 00:11:32.442
Okay.


00:11:34.944 --> 00:11:37.780
Have you ever been diagnosed
with any sleeping disorders?


00:11:37.864 --> 00:11:41.618
Uh, sleepwalking?
Night terrors? Insomnia?


00:11:41.701 --> 00:11:43.494
No.


00:11:45.622 --> 00:11:47.624
Not officially.


00:11:47.707 --> 00:11:51.377
I used to sleepwalk as a
kid, but I haven't in years.


00:11:51.461 --> 00:11:53.296
Okay.


00:11:58.092 --> 00:12:00.803
And you'll be okay to attend
for the full two-month period?


00:12:00.887 --> 00:12:03.306
- Yes.
- Perfect.


00:12:07.936 --> 00:12:09.562
Great.


00:12:14.859 --> 00:12:17.570
So, we really just show up and sleep?


00:12:17.654 --> 00:12:19.822
Yeah. That's it.


00:12:19.948 --> 00:12:23.243
Well, uh, we'll have you
hooked up to a bunch of stuff


00:12:23.368 --> 00:12:24.786
and ask you a few
questions every morning.


00:12:24.869 --> 00:12:26.162
But other than that...


00:12:26.287 --> 00:12:29.749
we just need you lying there in REM.


00:12:29.832 --> 00:12:32.043
REM?


00:12:32.126 --> 00:12:34.671
Uh, Rapid Eye Movement.


00:12:34.754 --> 00:12:38.341
It's the stage of sleep where
we dream the most vividly.


00:12:42.262 --> 00:12:44.138
Well, thanks for coming down, Sarah.


00:12:44.222 --> 00:12:46.349
I'll send your application
over to our head of faculty


00:12:46.432 --> 00:12:48.685
and we'll likely contact you tomorrow


00:12:48.768 --> 00:12:51.062
if you're chosen to
be a part of the study.


00:12:51.145 --> 00:12:52.814
When would we be starting?


00:12:52.897 --> 00:12:54.774
Uh, Monday.


00:12:54.857 --> 00:12:56.025
I hope to see you then.


00:12:56.109 --> 00:12:57.986
Okay, bye.


00:13:11.416 --> 00:13:13.334
What?


00:13:13.459 --> 00:13:15.420
You okay?


00:13:15.545 --> 00:13:16.921
Yeah. I'm good.


00:13:17.005 --> 00:13:18.798
Really?


00:13:18.881 --> 00:13:20.508
Really.


00:13:20.591 --> 00:13:22.885
'Cause, you know, it
would be okay if you weren't.


00:13:22.969 --> 00:13:24.762
I know.


00:13:41.738 --> 00:13:44.407
You have no idea how good this feels.


00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:47.493
Just to be in a bed and...


00:13:47.577 --> 00:13:48.661
in a house.


00:13:48.786 --> 00:13:51.581
Thank you.


00:13:58.421 --> 00:14:00.131
Goodnight.


00:14:00.256 --> 00:14:02.675
Mm. Sweet dreams.


00:16:37.622 --> 00:16:39.581
Can't believe it took
me this long to figure out


00:16:39.665 --> 00:16:43.461
how to make money when sleeping.


00:16:43.544 --> 00:16:44.878
I'm sure your wife is more than happy


00:16:44.962 --> 00:16:46.297
with the peace and quiet.


00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:48.716
Well, I know I am.


00:16:55.431 --> 00:16:57.308
Um, are, uh...


00:16:57.391 --> 00:17:00.186
are you the only girl in this study?


00:17:00.311 --> 00:17:01.770
Uh, no, there's another
in my room. Emily.


00:17:01.854 --> 00:17:03.397
Oh, cool.


00:17:03.481 --> 00:17:06.025
Is this your first sleeping clinic?


00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:07.777
Yup.


00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:09.070
You guys?


00:17:09.153 --> 00:17:10.738
Yeah.


00:17:10.821 --> 00:17:12.198
I've done a couple.


00:17:13.991 --> 00:17:15.660
Oh, hey.


00:17:27.046 --> 00:17:28.714
What about you?


00:17:28.798 --> 00:17:29.757
I've, uh...


00:17:29.882 --> 00:17:32.510
I've been coming to these
things since I was five.


00:17:32.593 --> 00:17:37.098
Aaron and I actually go way back.


00:17:37.181 --> 00:17:39.433
I was 16 when I first
started coming here.


00:17:41.352 --> 00:17:44.355
I guess ol' Meyer loves to see us sleep.


00:17:48.401 --> 00:17:49.318
Meyer?


00:17:49.402 --> 00:17:51.028
Doctor Meyer. He's, uh...


00:17:51.153 --> 00:17:53.489
He's head of the department.
You guys will meet him later.


00:17:53.573 --> 00:17:56.409
He, uh, usually does the exit interviews.


00:18:19.682 --> 00:18:21.434
Perfect fit.


00:18:21.559 --> 00:18:23.853
Come, sit down and
we'll get your headset on.


00:18:29.525 --> 00:18:31.068
Everyone has to wear these?


00:18:31.152 --> 00:18:33.112
I'm afraid so.


00:18:33.195 --> 00:18:35.906
It's how we get the information from you


00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:38.868
over to us in the control room.


00:18:41.912 --> 00:18:43.873
Okay...


00:19:13.778 --> 00:19:15.071
Excuse me?


00:19:15.154 --> 00:19:16.572
Hi, sorry, um...


00:19:16.697 --> 00:19:19.533
Michael told me to come down this way.


00:19:19.617 --> 00:19:20.493
Yeah, hi, Emily.


00:19:20.618 --> 00:19:22.244
You're in the right place, don't worry.


00:19:22.328 --> 00:19:23.579
You can just have a seat and
I'll be with you in one second.


00:19:23.663 --> 00:19:25.915
Okay. Thank you.


00:19:31.087 --> 00:19:33.047
- Hi.
- Hey.


00:19:37.468 --> 00:19:38.802
How many of us are in the study?


00:19:38.886 --> 00:19:44.308
Uh, six. Two females and four males.


00:19:44.433 --> 00:19:47.478
How come there's more guys?


00:19:47.561 --> 00:19:50.815
I can't tell you that.


00:19:50.898 --> 00:19:52.566
Well, what are you studying?


00:19:52.692 --> 00:19:55.069
I can't tell you that either.


00:19:58.531 --> 00:20:00.074
I told you to hurry.


00:20:00.199 --> 00:20:02.118
Well, Riff had me
installing the new drivers.


00:20:02.201 --> 00:20:03.869
It's okay. You can watch me do Emily's,


00:20:03.953 --> 00:20:06.038
and then I'll get you to help
apply the guys' next door.


00:20:06.122 --> 00:20:07.498
- Cool.
- Okay.


00:20:07.581 --> 00:20:10.376
- Hi.
- Hey.


00:20:10.501 --> 00:20:11.544
I'll get Sarah up and running


00:20:11.627 --> 00:20:12.878
so you can start with Emily now.


00:20:12.962 --> 00:20:14.922
Great. Thank you.


00:20:20.094 --> 00:20:22.388
- I'll be right back.
- Okay.


00:20:31.689 --> 00:20:34.275
You're almost set.


00:20:48.956 --> 00:20:50.708
How long till we're ready to go?


00:20:50.833 --> 00:20:52.460
I'd say about another hour


00:20:52.543 --> 00:20:54.628
before everyone's connected and settled.


00:20:54.712 --> 00:20:57.214
Okay. Great.


00:21:13.522 --> 00:21:15.691
Stage one,


00:21:15.775 --> 00:21:19.695
the eyes close.


00:21:19.779 --> 00:21:25.117
A reduction in activity
between wakefulness.


00:21:25.242 --> 00:21:28.537
The patient can be
awakened without difficulty,


00:21:28.621 --> 00:21:30.581
but if woken at this stage,


00:21:30.664 --> 00:21:33.876
the person will not feel
as if they have slept.


00:21:36.504 --> 00:21:38.255
Many have a feeling of falling


00:21:38.339 --> 00:21:41.342
during the first five to
ten minutes of sleep,


00:21:41.425 --> 00:21:44.804
which can cause a sudden
muscle contraction called...?


00:21:44.887 --> 00:21:46.222
Hypnic myoclonia?


00:21:46.305 --> 00:21:48.307
Very good, Lyle.


00:21:48.390 --> 00:21:51.602
Now, watch the EEG and the EOG.


00:21:51.685 --> 00:21:54.230
Some of them are entering stage two.


00:21:56.899 --> 00:21:59.151
We'll now see some peaks and valleys


00:21:59.235 --> 00:22:01.237
indicating periods of muscle tone


00:22:01.320 --> 00:22:04.990
and muscle relaxation.


00:22:05.074 --> 00:22:08.285
The SYNC will also show
us a slowing of the heart rate


00:22:08.369 --> 00:22:12.039
and a decrease in core temperature.


00:22:12.122 --> 00:22:15.334
Their bodies are preparing
them for deep sleep.


00:22:23.008 --> 00:22:25.761
Stage three and four...


00:22:25.845 --> 00:22:27.680
Slow wave...


00:22:27.805 --> 00:22:31.934
Delta.


00:22:32.017 --> 00:22:34.520
Wake them now, and for a moment,


00:22:34.645 --> 00:22:37.064
they'll have no idea where they are.


00:22:39.775 --> 00:22:42.903
Now we wait.


00:22:42.987 --> 00:22:46.574
In a bit, we'll start seeing
some entry into REM.


00:23:03.799 --> 00:23:05.926
It's like clockwork.


00:23:06.010 --> 00:23:11.515
Yes. Well, for most people it is.


00:23:11.599 --> 00:23:13.851
Are we ready?


00:23:13.934 --> 00:23:15.853
Recording.


00:23:33.120 --> 00:23:36.040
There.


00:23:36.123 --> 00:23:38.292
Whose feed is that?


00:23:40.544 --> 00:23:43.797
That's in A. Sarah Dunn.


00:24:37.559 --> 00:24:41.772
And... do you feel well rested?


00:24:41.855 --> 00:24:44.692
Yeah, I do actually.


00:24:44.775 --> 00:24:46.568
Uh, more rested or less rested


00:24:46.652 --> 00:24:50.531
than you usually feel
when sleeping at home?


00:24:50.614 --> 00:24:53.242
Definitely more rested.


00:24:53.367 --> 00:24:54.451
That's great.


00:24:54.576 --> 00:24:56.203
Now just a few more questions


00:24:56.286 --> 00:24:57.496
and then we'll be done for today.


00:24:57.579 --> 00:24:59.456
Okay.


00:25:46.879 --> 00:25:48.714
That good, huh?


00:26:19.536 --> 00:26:21.997
I read that in one sitting.


00:26:22.081 --> 00:26:23.624
Hm.


00:26:23.707 --> 00:26:27.336
Couldn't put it down.


00:26:27.419 --> 00:26:30.756
It's really good.


00:26:30.839 --> 00:26:32.216
Yeah?


00:26:32.299 --> 00:26:34.551
Hm. There's a...


00:26:34.635 --> 00:26:36.887
a kind of...


00:26:36.970 --> 00:26:38.639
a haunting sadness to it.


00:26:38.722 --> 00:26:41.183
You should definitely buy it.


00:26:41.266 --> 00:26:43.769
Have you read much Philip K. Dick?


00:26:43.852 --> 00:26:46.396
No, not... not much.


00:26:46.480 --> 00:26:49.358
He was completely paranoid.


00:26:49.441 --> 00:26:51.110
Genius concepts, though.


00:26:54.279 --> 00:26:58.408
His stuff will make you think.


00:26:58.492 --> 00:27:00.077
Thanks.


00:27:00.160 --> 00:27:02.287
I'll give him a try.


00:27:02.371 --> 00:27:04.748
You won't be sorry.


00:28:02.848 --> 00:28:03.849
You have to get me a job there


00:28:03.932 --> 00:28:05.350
because I'm practically
a professional sleeper!


00:28:05.434 --> 00:28:07.603
If I got paid to sleep,
I can't even imagine...


00:28:07.686 --> 00:28:08.353
Wait, wait. Wait, wait, wait.


00:28:08.478 --> 00:28:09.855
What?


00:28:09.938 --> 00:28:10.939
I'm trying to avoid that guy.


00:28:11.023 --> 00:28:12.357
- Who?
- The...


00:28:12.441 --> 00:28:15.194
Up there in the trench
coat and the glasses.


00:28:15.277 --> 00:28:17.112
I met him in a bookstore earlier.


00:28:17.196 --> 00:28:18.739
I just...


00:28:18.822 --> 00:28:20.532
I just don't feel like being
social, okay? Come on.


00:28:20.616 --> 00:28:24.119
Okay.


00:28:24.203 --> 00:28:26.622
You like him.


00:28:26.705 --> 00:28:28.749
Shut up!


00:28:31.376 --> 00:28:34.087
Okay, lie down.


00:28:39.343 --> 00:28:40.510
All set.


00:28:40.594 --> 00:28:44.765
Um, Anita will be by in a bit.


00:28:44.890 --> 00:28:46.558
Is Emily coming tonight?


00:28:46.642 --> 00:28:49.353
Uh, she's probably just running late.


00:28:49.478 --> 00:28:50.771
Or dropped out.


00:28:50.896 --> 00:28:55.192
It happens all the time on these things.


00:28:55.317 --> 00:28:57.736
Goodnight, Sarah.


00:28:57.861 --> 00:29:00.948
'Night.


00:31:31.932 --> 00:31:34.976
And... this one?


00:31:40.190 --> 00:31:42.109
No.


00:31:42.192 --> 00:31:44.194
Nothing.


00:31:44.277 --> 00:31:48.573
So, you have no reaction
to this image, correct?


00:31:48.657 --> 00:31:50.617
Correct.


00:31:50.700 --> 00:31:52.327
Okay.


00:31:57.082 --> 00:32:00.836
To be honest, I can't really
tell what any of these are.


00:32:00.961 --> 00:32:03.171
Yes, we know.


00:32:03.255 --> 00:32:06.633
Bear with us.


00:32:18.520 --> 00:32:20.313
I still don't really see or...


00:32:20.439 --> 00:32:23.442
or feel anything.


00:32:34.536 --> 00:32:37.831
Uh...


00:32:37.914 --> 00:32:41.668
I mean... some hands,
maybe, holding something?


00:33:00.687 --> 00:33:04.149
Is Emily still in the study?


00:33:04.274 --> 00:33:07.027
Probably not.


00:33:07.152 --> 00:33:09.654
Is something wrong?


00:33:09.738 --> 00:33:11.198
No.


00:33:11.281 --> 00:33:14.826
People usually lose interest
after the first couple nights.


00:33:14.910 --> 00:33:17.870
You know, realize they don't
like sleeping in a strange place


00:33:17.954 --> 00:33:19.623
or whatever, but...


00:33:19.706 --> 00:33:21.833
we'll have a replacement in
Room A as soon as we can.


00:33:21.917 --> 00:33:26.671
So you... you... you
talked to her, right?


00:33:26.796 --> 00:33:28.173
No.


00:33:28.256 --> 00:33:31.968
But this happens all the time.


00:33:32.052 --> 00:33:33.887
There are no-shows in
every cycle. It's just part...


00:33:33.970 --> 00:33:36.223
Guys...


00:33:36.306 --> 00:33:38.183
I'm sorry, but we have
four more of these to do


00:33:38.266 --> 00:33:40.310
until I get to go home and sleep.


00:33:46.149 --> 00:33:49.903
Okay, Sarah. Last one for today.


00:34:11.967 --> 00:34:13.718
Sarah?


00:34:13.843 --> 00:34:15.011
Sarah, are you...?


00:34:15.136 --> 00:34:17.055
Get Riff! Hurry!


00:34:35.031 --> 00:34:37.659
Is she okay?


00:34:37.742 --> 00:34:39.494
She seems to be now.


00:34:46.710 --> 00:34:48.461
No...


00:35:03.101 --> 00:35:05.353
I wasn't following you.


00:35:05.437 --> 00:35:08.148
Really?


00:35:08.231 --> 00:35:11.776
Then how come I kept
seeing you everywhere?


00:35:11.901 --> 00:35:15.697
Hm...


00:35:15.780 --> 00:35:17.741
You were sitting there...


00:35:17.824 --> 00:35:20.410
watching me sleep.


00:35:20.493 --> 00:35:22.287
And you just thought, "Hey..."


00:35:22.370 --> 00:35:25.123
"Since I don't ever leave my nerd den,"


00:35:25.206 --> 00:35:28.126
"this is probably my best chance
to meet the future Mrs. Nerd,"


00:35:28.209 --> 00:35:30.462
"so if I just follow her around,"


00:35:30.587 --> 00:35:33.965
"maybe she'll fall for my
magical fucking nerd charms!"


00:35:45.352 --> 00:35:49.272
Please don't quit our study
on account of my actions.


00:35:49.356 --> 00:35:55.111
I'm not quitting because of you.


00:35:55.195 --> 00:35:57.656
I'm quitting because I just
had the worst panic attack


00:35:57.739 --> 00:36:01.910
of my life and none of
you people will tell me why.


00:36:05.038 --> 00:36:06.331
Okay, Sarah.


00:36:06.414 --> 00:36:09.334
Last one for today.


00:36:10.835 --> 00:36:12.504
Sarah?


00:36:12.587 --> 00:36:13.713
Sarah, are you...?


00:36:13.797 --> 00:36:15.674
Get Riff! Hurry!


00:36:17.467 --> 00:36:19.469
And what did you think would happen


00:36:19.552 --> 00:36:23.473
when you showed these images to her?


00:36:23.556 --> 00:36:24.557
I...


00:36:24.641 --> 00:36:27.268
This isn't a joke, Anita.


00:36:27.352 --> 00:36:29.938
This is the first time
anyone has ever done this.


00:36:30.063 --> 00:36:32.898
And we have to be more than
careful about how it's handled.


00:36:32.982 --> 00:36:35.735
We'll either be hailed or crucified


00:36:35.860 --> 00:36:38.530
based on our treatment
of this breakthrough.


00:36:38.613 --> 00:36:39.989
We never...


00:36:40.073 --> 00:36:42.117
There's no more
unauthorized testing, Anita.


00:36:42.200 --> 00:36:44.786
I don't care what Riff says.


00:36:44.869 --> 00:36:47.831
We just wanted to see if they remember.


00:36:47.956 --> 00:36:50.458
Well, it's obvious that they do.


00:36:50.583 --> 00:36:52.836
So...


00:36:52.919 --> 00:36:55.964
let's go back to acting
like scientists again, okay?


00:36:56.089 --> 00:36:58.258
Now, that means collecting the data


00:36:58.341 --> 00:37:02.971
and then studying it within
the bounds of decency.


00:37:03.096 --> 00:37:08.226
We won't deviate from your methods again.


00:37:08.309 --> 00:37:11.312
Thank you.


00:37:11.396 --> 00:37:14.107
I'll be by later tonight to monitor.


00:38:03.907 --> 00:38:07.160
Hey.


00:38:07.243 --> 00:38:09.788
Zo?


00:38:14.083 --> 00:38:16.044
Hello?


00:38:40.235 --> 00:38:42.487
Young lady! Wake up! Wake up!


00:38:44.697 --> 00:38:46.699
I didn't want to wake
you, but those boys,


00:38:46.783 --> 00:38:49.035
they stole something from you.


00:38:49.118 --> 00:38:50.328
What?


00:38:50.411 --> 00:38:52.580
The boys, they took something from you,


00:38:52.705 --> 00:38:55.083
and then they ran off, so I woke you.


00:38:55.166 --> 00:38:59.504
How long was I...


00:38:59.629 --> 00:39:02.507
Fuck!


00:39:05.969 --> 00:39:10.306
Oh, no, no, no...


00:39:26.656 --> 00:39:30.743
Zoe? Zoe!


00:39:30.827 --> 00:39:34.038
Please be home. Please be home.


00:39:38.167 --> 00:39:41.379
Zo! Zo, come on!


00:39:41.462 --> 00:39:43.506
Zoe, come on, please.


00:39:55.268 --> 00:39:57.270
Hey, nerd!


00:40:03.943 --> 00:40:06.738
Hey.


00:40:06.821 --> 00:40:11.743
What were those pictures
Anita showed me this morning?


00:40:11.826 --> 00:40:14.913
I can't tell you that.


00:40:15.038 --> 00:40:17.832
I'm not coming back till you do.


00:40:17.957 --> 00:40:21.753
So, you're not quitting?


00:40:21.836 --> 00:40:25.465
I won't quit or tell anyone
you were stalking me...


00:40:25.548 --> 00:40:26.966
If... if...?


00:40:27.091 --> 00:40:29.302
If you tell me what you're studying.


00:40:29.427 --> 00:40:33.681
- It's not happening.
- Please.


00:40:33.765 --> 00:40:37.268
I'm starting to get scared, okay?


00:40:37.352 --> 00:40:41.189
Ever since this morning, it's...


00:40:41.272 --> 00:40:47.028
I have never felt so weird.


00:40:47.111 --> 00:40:48.696
But if I show you, it...


00:40:48.780 --> 00:40:50.573
it could completely
compromise the results...


00:40:50.657 --> 00:40:51.741
No, listen to me.


00:40:51.824 --> 00:40:54.827
I think your science
project is fucking me up!


00:40:58.915 --> 00:41:01.315
If I leave, doesn't that
compromise your results?


00:41:11.094 --> 00:41:13.846
All right, come on.


00:41:13.930 --> 00:41:15.890
Come on!


00:41:32.490 --> 00:41:35.535
I'm not kidding.


00:41:35.618 --> 00:41:39.205
If I show this to you...


00:41:39.288 --> 00:41:41.290
you cannot tell anyone.


00:41:51.134 --> 00:41:53.678
First off...


00:41:53.803 --> 00:41:56.639
you'll notice that I'm putting
this on my own head...


00:41:56.764 --> 00:41:57.932
so that you'll trust
me that there's nothing


00:41:58.016 --> 00:41:59.517
to be afraid of.


00:42:02.478 --> 00:42:05.523
Now, a few years ago,
some brilliant neuroscientist


00:42:05.606 --> 00:42:08.108
from Berkeley figured out
a way to decode the images


00:42:08.192 --> 00:42:10.111
our minds process...


00:42:10.236 --> 00:42:13.031
um, what we see...


00:42:13.114 --> 00:42:15.324
and export the data...


00:42:19.704 --> 00:42:22.790
...as a moving image.


00:42:26.210 --> 00:42:28.337
No way.


00:42:37.472 --> 00:42:38.890
That is so cool.


00:42:39.015 --> 00:42:42.894
It is!


00:42:46.189 --> 00:42:48.274
And... and I immediately thought
about where we could apply it.


00:42:48.357 --> 00:42:50.276
So I spent the last few
years tweaking this loaner


00:42:50.359 --> 00:42:54.322
to make it able to see
things even more amazing.


00:43:03.831 --> 00:43:07.168
You guys are watching our dreams?


00:43:07.251 --> 00:43:09.420
Yes!


00:43:20.473 --> 00:43:21.933
Obviously I can't show you yours,


00:43:22.016 --> 00:43:23.976
as we've already seen
what potentially happens


00:43:24.060 --> 00:43:29.065
when even a single frame
is recounted by the dreamer.


00:43:29.148 --> 00:43:31.859
I think I can safely cue up
a feed of someone else's


00:43:31.943 --> 00:43:33.528
from last night.


00:43:47.500 --> 00:43:49.877
Those are his dreams?


00:43:49.961 --> 00:43:51.671
No. No, he's still falling asleep.


00:43:51.754 --> 00:43:54.966
See?


00:43:55.091 --> 00:43:57.552
These are hypnagogic experiences.


00:43:57.635 --> 00:44:00.513
It's his brain trying to make
sense of the reduced input


00:44:00.638 --> 00:44:03.057
it's receiving as he loses consciousness.


00:44:06.018 --> 00:44:08.771
That is so weird.


00:44:08.855 --> 00:44:11.107
And fascinating.


00:44:11.190 --> 00:44:13.109
Look at the pictures and the shapes


00:44:13.192 --> 00:44:17.196
left floating around in his mind.


00:44:17.280 --> 00:44:20.199
It's actually quite beautiful.


00:44:30.001 --> 00:44:31.627
If I remember correctly, I...


00:44:31.711 --> 00:44:33.754
I think he had a pretty
scary dream off the top.


00:44:33.838 --> 00:44:36.507
I might have to cut it short.


00:45:56.337 --> 00:46:00.591
Are my dreams that messed up?


00:46:00.675 --> 00:46:03.886
Sometimes.


00:46:03.970 --> 00:46:05.221
We all have nightmares.


00:46:19.694 --> 00:46:23.030
This is nuts.


00:46:29.620 --> 00:46:31.789
Don't you ever feel like
you're seeing something


00:46:31.872 --> 00:46:34.125
that you're not supposed to?


00:46:35.793 --> 00:46:39.588
I... I wouldn't be doing this if
I didn't have a reason, Sarah.


00:46:42.300 --> 00:46:43.342
Which is?


00:46:46.429 --> 00:46:49.265
Fuck. Uh, we... we have to go.


00:46:49.348 --> 00:46:51.892
Come on.


00:46:59.567 --> 00:47:02.111
I held up my end...


00:47:12.663 --> 00:47:15.499
See you inside.


00:50:12.801 --> 00:50:14.470
That's new.


00:50:14.595 --> 00:50:16.972
It is.


00:50:17.056 --> 00:50:21.060
Let's clean it up a bit.


00:50:45.000 --> 00:50:47.628
How is this happening?


00:50:50.673 --> 00:50:52.550
They all have their own unique hypnagogic


00:50:52.633 --> 00:50:57.846
and narrative episodes, but eventually...


00:50:57.930 --> 00:51:00.474
they end up here like this.


00:51:22.079 --> 00:51:23.789
I've been seeing these
things in my own dreams


00:51:23.872 --> 00:51:26.917
since I was six years old.


00:51:27.001 --> 00:51:29.587
There's countless
records throughout history,


00:51:29.670 --> 00:51:31.922
across varying cultures
and yet for some reason


00:51:32.006 --> 00:51:35.801
we always figure out a way
to simply discount them as...


00:51:35.884 --> 00:51:37.678
just dreams.


00:51:40.639 --> 00:51:42.683
It's fucking scary


00:51:42.766 --> 00:51:45.894
finding what really makes us tick.


00:52:09.168 --> 00:52:11.670
Lyle, can you grab this in 4K?


00:52:24.099 --> 00:52:25.976
- Dunn's coming out of REM.
- Fuck!


00:52:26.060 --> 00:52:28.228
Her pulse is really fucking elevated.


00:52:50.959 --> 00:52:52.878
Sarah?


00:52:52.961 --> 00:52:54.088
Sarah!


00:53:01.762 --> 00:53:04.556
Sarah, are you okay?


00:53:04.682 --> 00:53:08.352
Fuck this place! No, I'm not okay!


00:53:08.435 --> 00:53:10.145
Look, you just had a nightmare.


00:53:10.229 --> 00:53:12.439
I know I had a nightmare!


00:53:14.900 --> 00:53:18.654
What was it about, Anita? Huh?


00:53:18.737 --> 00:53:20.531
Did you see them?


00:53:22.741 --> 00:53:25.703
Yeah, I know what you're
doing so you can shut the fuck up!


00:53:25.786 --> 00:53:27.162
I'm fucking done with this!


00:53:27.246 --> 00:53:30.624
I'll be right back. Keep
watching the others!


00:53:30.749 --> 00:53:33.460
Sarah!


00:53:33.544 --> 00:53:36.797
Your eye.


00:53:42.594 --> 00:53:44.638
What is going on, Riff?!


00:53:47.725 --> 00:53:49.893
- Nothing.
- Meyer's coming in at 2!


00:53:50.018 --> 00:53:51.103
What do I tell him?!


00:53:51.186 --> 00:53:53.397
Keep monitoring the others!
I'll be back before then!


00:55:49.805 --> 00:55:52.516
Bill!


00:55:52.599 --> 00:55:53.684
Is Zoe here tonight?


00:55:53.767 --> 00:55:54.893
Might be. I just got here.


00:55:54.977 --> 00:55:57.145
Can I go in and check?


00:56:09.908 --> 00:56:13.161
- He has two minutes.
- Yep.


00:56:13.287 --> 00:56:16.707
Then he's gonna explain
to us how she knew.


00:56:16.790 --> 00:56:20.252
Yes. He is.


00:56:20.335 --> 00:56:23.338
I think one of the
guys in C is waking up.


00:56:29.052 --> 00:56:30.512
It's Will.


00:56:30.637 --> 00:56:33.140
They're both waking up.


00:56:41.273 --> 00:56:42.900
No...


00:56:43.025 --> 00:56:45.360
Look at the room...


00:56:45.485 --> 00:56:47.154
Their vitals.


00:56:49.489 --> 00:56:52.367
It's happening.


00:56:58.165 --> 00:57:01.043
Lyle, get Riff. Right now!


00:57:11.386 --> 00:57:13.305
What's going on?


00:58:25.627 --> 00:58:26.586
Where's Riff again?


00:58:27.838 --> 00:58:29.089
He had to run home for something,


00:58:29.172 --> 00:58:31.842
but he should be back any minute.


00:58:33.343 --> 00:58:36.763
Well, I just don't want him to miss this.


00:58:36.847 --> 00:58:39.933
This is exactly what
he's been waiting for.


00:59:34.029 --> 00:59:35.864
Hey! Is she okay?


01:00:08.396 --> 01:00:10.941
I feel bad about having
them go through this.


01:00:11.066 --> 01:00:12.943
Must be horrible.


01:00:13.026 --> 01:00:15.362
It is.


01:00:15.445 --> 01:00:18.156
But this is a natural function.


01:00:18.240 --> 01:00:19.491
And if we're going to understand it,


01:00:19.574 --> 01:00:21.743
we need this data.


01:00:21.868 --> 01:00:23.870
These images...


01:00:23.954 --> 01:00:29.251
they prove a kind of a
primal connection to this icon.


01:00:29.334 --> 01:00:33.672
A unified fear of this shadow with eyes.


01:01:05.912 --> 01:01:09.166
Their vitals aren't changing.


01:01:09.291 --> 01:01:13.295
Discreetly get in there and
re-connect their SYNCS.


01:01:13.420 --> 01:01:15.505
Should we wake them?


01:01:32.647 --> 01:01:34.983
There.


01:01:54.502 --> 01:01:55.629
No fuckin' way.


01:01:55.754 --> 01:01:57.797
What?


01:02:04.429 --> 01:02:05.055
Michael...


01:02:05.180 --> 01:02:07.807
Michael, what is it?


01:07:59.951 --> 01:08:02.328
♪ They can ♪


01:08:02.412 --> 01:08:05.957
♪ Say what they say ♪


01:08:06.040 --> 01:08:09.502
♪ But you need a heart ♪


01:08:09.586 --> 01:08:15.258
♪ To have heart like you do ♪


01:08:15.341 --> 01:08:17.969
♪ You're too ♪


01:08:18.052 --> 01:08:21.389
♪ You're too careful ♪


01:08:21.472 --> 01:08:25.310
♪ To truly not care ♪


01:08:25.393 --> 01:08:30.773
♪ I don't believe that it's true ♪


01:08:30.898 --> 01:08:36.821
♪ Oh, you might shed some tears ♪


01:08:36.904 --> 01:08:40.783
♪ But these modern fears ♪


01:08:40.867 --> 01:08:46.331
♪ Won't hold you down ♪


01:08:46.456 --> 01:08:52.462
♪ And, oh, it might take some years ♪


01:08:52.545 --> 01:08:56.466
♪ But these modern fears ♪


01:08:56.549 --> 01:08:59.677
♪ Won't be around ♪


01:09:05.933 --> 01:09:12.148
♪ How can you be modest ♪


01:09:12.273 --> 01:09:16.152
♪ When you know that ♪


01:09:16.235 --> 01:09:21.532
♪ That you're number one ♪


01:09:21.616 --> 01:09:24.494
♪ I know ♪


01:09:24.619 --> 01:09:27.997
♪ You're not over ♪


01:09:28.081 --> 01:09:31.959
♪ Even if they think ♪


01:09:32.043 --> 01:09:37.423
♪ This time you're done ♪


01:09:37.548 --> 01:09:43.221
♪ Oh, you might shed some tears ♪


01:09:43.304 --> 01:09:47.183
♪ But these modern fears ♪


01:09:47.266 --> 01:09:52.397
♪ Won't hold you down ♪


01:09:52.480 --> 01:09:58.861
♪ And, oh, it might take some years ♪


01:09:58.945 --> 01:10:03.032
♪ But these modern fears ♪


01:10:03.157 --> 01:10:07.203
♪ Won't be around ♪


01:11:24.071 --> 01:11:25.364
Wake up!


01:11:25.448 --> 01:11:29.076
Wake up! Wake up!


01:11:29.202 --> 01:11:31.621
You gotta wake up! You gotta wake up!


01:11:51.474 --> 01:11:53.518
Hey.


01:11:53.643 --> 01:11:56.687
Hey.


01:13:00.042 --> 01:13:01.919
Um, I'll be right back.


01:13:40.499 --> 01:13:43.169
Oh, weird question.


01:13:43.294 --> 01:13:46.005
Can I sleep on your couch tonight?


01:13:48.633 --> 01:13:50.760
Of course.


01:13:50.885 --> 01:13:54.472
I lost my phone.


01:13:54.555 --> 01:13:57.642
And I have nowhere else to go.


01:14:19.038 --> 01:14:21.165
Why "Riff"?


01:14:23.042 --> 01:14:25.086
You ever see the Rocky Horror?


01:14:25.169 --> 01:14:27.922
Of course.


01:14:28.005 --> 01:14:33.219
You remember Riff-Raff?


01:14:33.302 --> 01:14:35.930
Oh...


01:14:36.013 --> 01:14:39.350
I get it. You're Meyer's Igor.


01:14:43.854 --> 01:14:45.481
You know, you're smart for your age.


01:14:45.564 --> 01:14:47.566
I'm 18.


01:14:56.951 --> 01:15:00.037
I saw your dream.


01:15:10.589 --> 01:15:15.136
♪ 'Cause we're both misunderstood ♪


01:15:18.514 --> 01:15:21.934
♪ 'Cause we're both misunderstood ♪


01:16:48.395 --> 01:16:50.815
Sarah?


01:16:50.898 --> 01:16:53.025
Oh, Sarah...


01:17:11.544 --> 01:17:15.589
Are there any relatives,
next-of-kin we can contact?


01:17:15.673 --> 01:17:18.634
I don't know. I don't know her very well.


01:20:39.376 --> 01:20:41.962
Hello?!


01:20:42.046 --> 01:20:44.214
Nurse!


01:20:50.429 --> 01:20:52.306
Hello?!


01:21:00.314 --> 01:21:01.440
Where is everyone?


01:21:01.565 --> 01:21:03.067
On the second floor, I... I...


01:21:03.150 --> 01:21:04.401
I have a friend that's
being treated up there


01:21:04.485 --> 01:21:05.652
and I don't know where she is now.


01:21:05.736 --> 01:21:07.363
There's no nurses at the front desk.


01:21:07.446 --> 01:21:08.197
What's your friend's name?


01:21:08.322 --> 01:21:11.283
Dunn. Sarah Dunn.


01:21:11.367 --> 01:21:14.286
- Sarah...
- Dunn.


01:21:14.411 --> 01:21:16.246
Sarah... Dunn.


01:21:16.372 --> 01:21:18.957
She's in 237.


01:21:19.083 --> 01:21:20.250
No! No, she's not.


01:21:20.334 --> 01:21:22.127
She's... that's what I'm
telling you, she's not there!


01:21:22.211 --> 01:21:24.254
Sir, please calm down.


01:21:24.380 --> 01:21:26.590
We will find out where she is.


01:21:26.715 --> 01:21:27.341
Let me call a nurse on the second...


01:21:27.424 --> 01:21:28.884
But there's no one up there!


01:21:28.967 --> 01:21:30.719
I'm tell... I'm telling you.


01:21:42.064 --> 01:21:44.525
Jerry, can you run up to the second and


01:21:44.608 --> 01:21:46.568
find Rachel or Kiki for me?


01:21:46.693 --> 01:21:50.739
This gentleman's looking
for a patient's whereabouts.


01:21:50.823 --> 01:21:52.491
I told you there's no one up there.


01:21:52.574 --> 01:21:53.742
They probably had to move her


01:21:53.826 --> 01:21:55.702
due to tonight's staffing shortage.


01:21:55.828 --> 01:21:58.247
Um, why don't you take
a seat over by the desk


01:21:58.330 --> 01:22:02.167
and I'll give you a call when
we have her new location.


01:22:02.251 --> 01:22:04.002
Okay, thanks. I just...


01:22:04.086 --> 01:22:06.130
I'm... I'm just... I'm worried about her.


01:23:31.840 --> 01:23:34.468
Sarah!


01:23:37.721 --> 01:23:39.723
Sarah! It's me, Jeremy!


01:23:44.436 --> 01:23:46.897
Sarah!


01:23:59.826 --> 01:24:01.620
Sarah...


01:24:05.582 --> 01:24:07.167
Sarah...


01:24:12.631 --> 01:24:15.425
It's me, Jeremy.


01:24:15.509 --> 01:24:16.927
Wake up.


01:24:19.846 --> 01:24:22.391
Wake up.


01:24:25.811 --> 01:24:27.145
Augh!


01:24:44.955 --> 01:24:47.541
Where the fuck have you been?!


01:24:47.666 --> 01:24:50.001
Look, I can't explain right
now. Are you at the lab?


01:24:50.085 --> 01:24:53.589
Yes! I'm here and I'm
cleaning up your mess.


01:24:53.672 --> 01:24:55.799
I... I really need you right now.


01:24:55.882 --> 01:24:59.720
No! No! You have
fucked up all of our lives!


01:24:59.803 --> 01:25:01.304
We'll be lucky if we
ever do another study...


01:25:01.388 --> 01:25:02.639
I know, I'm sorry, it's just...


01:25:02.723 --> 01:25:04.224
something's happened
to Sarah Dunn and I...


01:25:04.308 --> 01:25:05.434
I just really need you to come out...


01:25:05.517 --> 01:25:08.312
What did you do?


01:25:10.522 --> 01:25:13.066
I really fucked up.


01:25:13.150 --> 01:25:16.612
Just one more thing and we're done.


01:25:16.737 --> 01:25:19.823
Anita, please.


01:25:19.948 --> 01:25:22.701
Then we're done.


01:26:58.630 --> 01:27:01.383
- What the fuck, Riff?!
- Where's the stuff?


01:27:01.466 --> 01:27:03.719
The trunk.


01:27:37.210 --> 01:27:39.045
Why don't we take her
back to the hospital?


01:27:39.129 --> 01:27:41.173
'Cause she's not safe there.


01:27:41.256 --> 01:27:42.382
They have no clue
what's happening to her.


01:27:42.466 --> 01:27:44.468
No more than we do.


01:27:48.013 --> 01:27:50.974
It's up.


01:28:04.571 --> 01:28:07.783
It's a nightmare.


01:28:07.866 --> 01:28:11.286
It's... it's good. It can
help us get her out.


01:28:11.369 --> 01:28:15.165
You keep watching her. I'll
make sure that she's safe.


01:29:05.715 --> 01:29:09.886
So, we try to wake her at
the height of her nightmare?


01:29:09.970 --> 01:29:12.472
Yes.


01:29:12.556 --> 01:29:14.391
The body tries to reject death in dreams.


01:29:14.474 --> 01:29:16.852
You wake up.


01:29:16.977 --> 01:29:20.856
What if you're wrong?


01:29:20.939 --> 01:29:23.441
I don't know.


01:30:00.186 --> 01:30:01.813
Anything?


01:30:01.938 --> 01:30:04.608
Nothing yet.


01:30:04.691 --> 01:30:07.611
Look, how much further should
we really let her continue...


01:30:07.694 --> 01:30:09.946
Whoa, whoa, whoa.


01:31:12.759 --> 01:31:14.886
This isn't making any sense.


01:31:14.970 --> 01:31:16.513
I thought she was headed
somewhere familiar, or...


01:31:16.596 --> 01:31:19.641
Wait! I see something.


01:31:51.631 --> 01:31:54.259
I've never seen or
dreamt of this many before.


01:31:56.720 --> 01:31:58.763
When one of them comes
close or touches her,


01:31:58.847 --> 01:32:01.182
she'll expel herself from the dream.


01:33:21.805 --> 01:33:23.890
Riff, I don't want to do this anymore.


01:33:23.973 --> 01:33:26.573
Let's call a cab, okay?
Let's get out of here, leave!


01:33:32.816 --> 01:33:34.609
Just... just keep watching.


01:34:28.121 --> 01:34:29.789
Sarah...


01:34:29.914 --> 01:34:32.292
Hey, I'm right here. I'm here.


01:34:32.375 --> 01:34:35.170
What happened?


01:34:35.253 --> 01:34:38.339
I'm so sorry. I'm so sorry.


01:34:38.423 --> 01:34:40.675
We couldn't wake you...


01:34:40.758 --> 01:34:42.218
We couldn't wake you.


01:34:42.343 --> 01:34:44.846
You saw?


01:34:44.929 --> 01:34:47.807
- You saw?
- Yes.


01:34:52.604 --> 01:34:54.814
I'm so sorry. I'm sorry.


01:34:57.483 --> 01:35:00.862
I'm so sorry. I'm so sorry.


01:35:33.686 --> 01:35:36.231
Are you certain this is
the way that we came in?


01:35:40.735 --> 01:35:43.738
Where did you get this?


01:35:43.821 --> 01:35:45.949
I found it out in the field.


01:35:46.074 --> 01:35:49.619
This is my phone.


01:35:49.702 --> 01:35:51.454
You lost it out here?


01:35:51.537 --> 01:35:53.206
I've never been here!


01:35:53.331 --> 01:35:55.458
Look, maybe you've had
an episode like this before


01:35:55.541 --> 01:35:58.544
- and you came and you dropped...
- What time is it?


01:36:03.591 --> 01:36:06.552
What the fuck?


01:36:06.678 --> 01:36:11.266
What time does it say it is?


01:36:39.585 --> 01:36:43.047
Run!


01:36:48.636 --> 01:36:51.389
No! No...


01:36:56.936 --> 01:36:58.187
Just keep breathing.


01:37:01.399 --> 01:37:03.359
No...!


01:42:38.361 --> 01:42:40.905
♪ They can ♪


01:42:40.988 --> 01:42:45.117
♪ Say what they say ♪


01:42:45.201 --> 01:42:48.412
♪ But you need a heart ♪


